DTSTAMP:20261025T041905Z
SUMMARY:Sartorius Table Show
DTSTART:20261112T150000Z
DTEND:20261112T170000Z
LOCATION:UF Innovate | Sid Martin Biotech\, 12085 Research Dr.\, Alachua\, 
 FL 32615
URL:https://calendar.ufl.edu/innovate/event/58453-sartorius-table-show
DESCRIPTION:Sartorius is pleased to connect with the Sid Martin community t
 o discuss how their expertise\, technologies\, and application support can
  help advance stem cell\, immune cell\, and other advanced-therapy workflo
 ws.\nSartorius supports academic innovators and early-stage biotechnology 
 companies as they move promising research toward scalable\, reproducible p
 rocesses. Their portfolio includes solutions for cell culture\, cell and g
 ene therapy development\, bioprocessing\, analytical workflows\, and labor
 atory applications. They work collaboratively with researchers and emergin
 g biotech teams to help address evolving needs from early research and pro
 cess development through scale-up and manufacturing readiness.About our sp
 eaker:Sean Griffin\nSean Griffin is a Technical Sales Specialist in Cell T
 herapy within the Advanced Therapies Solutions division at Sartorius\, sup
 porting innovative technologies and solutions that advance cell therapy de
 velopment and manufacturing.About Sartorius:\nWe are living in the bio-cen
 tury\, where global medical knowledge is expanding at a rapid pace. Howeve
 r\, despite significant breakthroughs\, many diseases\, including cancer\,
  rheumatism\, and Alzheimer’s\, remain incurable.\nSartorius is part of 
 the solution\, helping ensure that new scientific discoveries can be trans
 lated more quickly into effective patient care. Through innovative technol
 ogies\, platforms\, and partnerships\, Sartorius works toward a common goa
 l: better health for more people.\n Thank you to our sponsors:\n\n ——
 —————UF Innovate | Accelerate\nUF Innovate | Accelerate is the U
 niversity of Florida’s entrepreneurship support program that includes Si
 d Martin Biotech\, the globally recognized biotechnology incubator located
  in Progress Park in Alachua\, Florida\, and The Hub\, the globally recogn
 ized diversified tech incubator located in Gainesville’s Innovation Dist
 rict.\nHosted by: UF Innovate\nUF Innovate: https://calendar.ufl.edu/innov
 ate/event/58453-sartorius-table-show\nstartGNV: https://startgnv.com/event
 /sartorius-table-show/
END:VEVENT
